# Close-out C3: a suspended user's test-send is refused (409, an answer that does not say why) BEFORE the worker seam is touched. The fault deletes that gate from the test-send handler: the suspended user's request then reaches the sender and answers 202. The real handler is driven over real HTTP against real Postgres with a counting TestSender and a suspended user, and must answer the opaque 409 with ZERO sender calls; the same request after reinstatement (the paired control) must succeed. The CMD builds the migrated template database on the stock postgres service first, as tests/harness/run.sh does.
GATE=m3-suspension-gate
TARGET=module:coldmail-send-byo
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestSuspensionGate_TestSendIsRefusedWhileSuspendedAndZeroSenderCalls (a suspended user's test-send over real HTTP, real Postgres)
CMD=T=fp_m3_p2c_tpl; TPL="${FAULT_ADMIN_DSN%/*}/$T"; psql "$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -q -c "DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS $T" -c "CREATE DATABASE $T" && psql "$TPL" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -q -c "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.users(id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), email text, is_active boolean default true, created_at timestamptz default now())" -c "CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.job_items(id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(), campaign_id uuid, user_id uuid, recipient_email text, rendered_subject text, rendered_body text, reply_to text, status text, created_at timestamptz default now())" && (cd tools/send-byo-migrate && go build -o bin/send-byo-migrate .) && MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL="$TPL" SEND_BYO_MODULE_PASSWORD=devmodulepass tools/send-byo-migrate/bin/send-byo-migrate up-and-set-password && cd services/control && TEST_ADMIN_DATABASE_URL="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" TEST_TEMPLATE_DB="$T" SEND_BYO_MODULE_PASSWORD=devmodulepass go test -count=1 -v -run '^TestSuspensionGate_TestSendIsRefusedWhileSuspendedAndZeroSenderCalls$' ./internal/platformapi/
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestSuspensionGate_TestSendIsRefusedWhileSuspendedAndZeroSenderCalls
MESSAGE=status=202, want 409
